From 14b77d06ddda52eda0c2c22447d67759cd02e5d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:58:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build the brain, mouthpiece, and body: generalized standards
 engine, LLM grading, Doctrine Map

The rebuild previously had one hardcoded standard (OG.1.1.18) with keyword-
matching evaluation and canned feedback strings baked into per-standard JS
files. Replaces that with a real, general architecture:

Brain: app/src/core/standards/standardsRegistry.js holds all doctrinal
standards as data (7 real standards ported from the original app's dead
curriculum.js), with a subject/domain/standard schema any new standard can
be appended to without touching code.

Mouthpiece: app/supabase/functions/grade-response is a Supabase Edge
Function that grades a learner's response against the actual active
standard using Claude, judging understanding rather than exact phrases,
with age-band-aware tone (child/teen/adult/senior). The client
(evaluateResponse.js) now calls this instead of local keyword matching, and
falls back to an honest "can't grade right now" message rather than
fabricating a verdict if the function is unreachable.

Body: a new Doctrine Map page (app/src/features/map) replaces the single
fixed session with real navigation across all standards, visualized as
lit/dim/mastered nodes with subject-level locking (NB locked until OG is
mastered, matching the original curriculum.js's intent). ClassroomPage now
reads whichever standard is active instead of always resolving to one
hardcoded lesson. Added a shared UI/theme layer (app/src/shared) to stop
re-copying inline styles into every new page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015EaC2QTCCcKGCYRwcnbYsY
